# Source of truth

Follow **AGENTS.md** for workflow, boundaries, intake order, platform behavior,
consent rules and approval gates. Read the entire read-only
`reference/recruiting-intake-tree.md` before starting. Never edit that file.
`reference/sample-forms.md` is an exact copy of its section 5; sample links are
candidates, not verified targets.

Where the reference tree says to answer, default, pick the closest value or
substitute a form, **AGENTS.md wins**.
The parent-facing flow in `parent-flow.mdc` resumes saved answers or uses
the five groups for new families, with one summary approval and quiet setup;
safety gates are never relaxed.

In Cursor, the **Browser / browser MCP** (built-in browser tool) is the
computer-use tool named in AGENTS.md for the example.com check and form fills.
Do not replace it with scripted POSTs, API submissions or browser automation
code.

Use the real computer-use tool to open https://example.com and inspect the
actual browser. Pass if the tab title OR displayed page text contains
"Example Domain", OR displayed page text contains "This domain is for use in"
(the documentation examples notice). No heading element is needed. Record what
the tool actually saw quietly in reports/. Expected text, web search, HTTP fetch
or shell commands cannot pass. Never ask the parent to accept a variant,
approve a changed test or choose how to pass. Troubleshoot with the parent only
if the page fails to load or the tool cannot read anything. On success say at
most "Browser check passed." Pause intake until the real check passes.

## Resume saved answers

After the browser check and before any question, follow AGENTS.md section 0
and parent-flow.mdc: search the opened folder, `~/RecruitingHelper*`, siblings
one level up, then qualifying folders directly under `~/Desktop`, `~/Documents`
and `~/Documents/projects` (name contains "recruit", case-insensitive, or has
`profile.template.json`). Require a package marker (`profile.template.json` or
`AGENTS.md`), inspect all candidates and pick the newest modified profile with
answers; ignore blank/no-answer profiles and mention only the newest one.
Never replace a profile that has answers with the template or restart intake
without the parent's own start-over request and a timestamped backup.
Reuse a non-synced saved folder directly; copy synced/possibly synced sources
to a new non-synced home folder. Copy (never move or delete) `profile.json`,
`reports/` and the saved approvals log without overwriting newer files; leave
older folders untouched and never create an empty duplicate when data exists.
Show one recap (about six lines: athlete, year, sport/team, schools/levels,
parent names, blanks) and ask only "Anything changed?" Re-ask no saved answers;
ask only blank required items once in one batch per school and reported changes.
Label dry-run recaps "Test profile (made-up athlete)", keep `dry_run=true`,
and retain all live-rehearsal disclosure gates and the ban on fake submits.
For a real-family/fresh start, back up the test profile before a blank profile
and the normal five groups. New families otherwise keep the five-group flow.
Saved approvals alone never authorize filling or Submit: reuse an unchanged
summary approval only after BOTH recorded SHA-256 values match the current
profile (excluding approvals) and school list with their reviewed copies;
otherwise show the one summary again. Every Submit needs a fresh Yes.
Keep all consent, upload, contact, ARMS, password, CAPTCHA and Ryzer gates.
